Patch: zoneInfoCache
Letter: C
Requires: none
Files: src/impl/locale.js, src/impl/util.js
Summary: parseZoneInfo: reuse the existing DTF cache instead of building one per call

C: parseZoneInfo builds a new Intl.DateTimeFormat per call

Nothing caches it, so any format carrying a zone name (ZZZZ/ZZZZZ, or the
offsetNameShort/offsetNameLong getters) pays a formatter construction per
value. Profiling puts this at ~73% of the total cost of formatting a column
with an abbreviation. The formatter depends only on (locale, offsetFormat,
timeZone), and luxon already has a DTF cache with exactly those semantics —
getCachedDTF, which Locale.resetCache() clears.

Upstream caveat: parseZoneInfo lives in impl/util.js while getCachedDTF lives
in impl/locale.js, and locale.js already imports util.js — so the import this
patch adds closes a cycle. It resolves correctly, because getCachedDTF is a
hoisted function declaration and its binding is live before either module body
runs, and the benchmarks confirm it loads and formats under both node and bun.
A PR would still more likely move parseZoneInfo down into locale.js, or the DTF
cache up into util.js, rather than ask a reviewer to accept the cycle.

